.TH TLLAMA 1 "October 2026" "TLlama" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tllama \- command-line client for a TLlama or Ollama-compatible server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tllama
.RI [ options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tllama
connects to an existing server. With no command it displays help.
It does not launch a daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list, ls
List available models.
.TP
.B show MODEL
Show a model's definition and metadata.
.TP
.B ps
List loaded models.
.TP
.B pull MODEL
Download a model through the selected server.
.TP
.B rm MODEL...
Remove model definitions.
.TP
.B stop MODEL
Unload a model.
.TP
.B run MODEL [PROMPT...]
Run inference, or open an interactive prompt when no prompt or redirected
input is supplied. Enter /help for interactive commands.
.TP
.B cp SOURCE DESTINATION
Copy a model definition.
.TP
.B create MODEL -f FILE
Create a model from a TOML definition. Referenced client input files use the
client working directory unless their paths are absolute.
.TP
.B version
Show version information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config PATH
Read only this client TOML file over built-in defaults, excluding system and
user configuration files.
.TP
.B --host ADDRESS
Server address; overrides TLLAMA_HOST. Default: http://127.0.0.1:54800.
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Override the request timeout policy.
.TP
.B --json
Use machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --decimal-units, --no-decimal-units
Select decimal kB/MB/GB/TB or binary KiB/MiB/GiB/TiB for human sizes. Binary is
the default. API and JSON byte values are unchanged.
.TP
.B run MODEL --verbose, -v, --no-verbose
Override the default display of request timing and token statistics on stderr.
.TP
.B run MODEL --hide-thinking, --show-thinking
Hide or show reasoning text for completion models. This changes display only,
not generation controls, conversation messages or JSON events.
.TP
.B run MODEL --option KEY=VALUE
Set a request option; repeatable, with the last value for a key winning.
VALUE uses JSON syntax, for example num_ctx=32768 or temperature=0.7.
Load-time options are included in the first interactive preload, avoiding
a default-context load followed by a reload merely to change the context.
.TP
.B --help
Show help. Each command has its own --help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed client version.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/tllama/client.toml
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tllama/client.toml
(default: ~/.config/tllama/client.toml)
.PP
System settings are read first, then individual user settings override them.
The [client] table accepts host and timeout. The [display] table accepts
decimal_units, hide_thinking and verbose (booleans, default false).
CLI options override environment
settings, which override file settings. Missing automatic files are ignored;
invalid or unreadable files and missing explicit files are errors.
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/tllama/docs/cli.md
.SH PROCESS DIAGNOSTICS
ps --json returns the compact server summary. ps --detailed --json requests
the complete TLlama memory and lifecycle diagnostics. --detailed requires --json.
.SH INTERACTIVE HISTORY
REPL inputs persist separately per server and model in XDG_STATE_HOME/tllama/history
(normally ~/.local/state/tllama/history). Files are private to the user.
Use [history] enabled=false in client.toml or run --no-history to disable
persistence. run --clear-history removes saved inputs for this scope before
opening the REPL. Input history does not restore conversation messages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tllamad (1)
